# T9 (docs/plans/editor-ux-redesign.md): hello world's journey through the GUI
# alone (RWSMAN_CORPUS=<unpacked game>, RWSMAN_HELLO_WORLD=<its project>, for
# the terrain). A new project in the Convoy slot gets hello world's terrain,
# its imports, players, props, cover, guards, dog, walk grid, zones,
# objectives, equipment, tips and a five-shot intro, all by clicks in the
# viewport, the Outliner and the panels; then it is saved and reopened.
#
# The result has hello world's structure, not its bytes: the same actors,
# zones, dummies and scripts, every event raised and no problems. It differs
# where the GUI works differently: the players get no start group (so one
# navigation group fewer), the walk grid keeps clear of props in its own way,
# IDs are the next free ones and positions are where the clicks land.
require RWSMAN_CORPUS
require RWSMAN_HELLO_WORLD
remove $UI_OUTPUT/HelloE2E
resize 1600x1200
setting resource_root $RWSMAN_CORPUS
setting projects_root $UI_OUTPUT
click "New project..."
click "New project::new_project_name"
key Ctrl+A
type HelloE2E
click "New project::Create"
wait idle
expect project.slot Convoy
# The terrain, as Blender's Send writes it: hello world's; then Rebuild map.
copy $RWSMAN_HELLO_WORLD/sources/world HelloE2E/sources/world
command mission.project_rebuild
wait idle
# Classes and animations from other missions, through the import form.
click "Assets::Import a class without placing it"
click Assets::##donor
type $RWSMAN_CORPUS/Escape
click Assets::##import_filter
key Ctrl+A
type "484  "
click Assets::import_484
click Assets::##import_filter
key Ctrl+A
type "383  "
click Assets::import_383
click Assets::##donor
key Ctrl+A
type $RWSMAN_CORPUS/Ransom
click Assets::##import_filter
key Ctrl+A
type "431  "
click Assets::import_431
click Assets::##import_anim
key Ctrl+A
type 2383
click "Assets::Import animation"
click Assets::##import_anim
key Ctrl+A
type 2384
click "Assets::Import animation"
click "Assets::Import a class without placing it"
